","name":"component/ui","color":"0052cc","default":false,"description":null},{"id":647013637,"node_id":"MDU6TGFiZWw2NDcwMTM2Mzc=","url":"https://api.github.com/repos/prometheus/prometheus/labels/priority/P3","name":"priority/P3","color":"fbca04","default":false,"description":null}],"state":"closed","locked":true,"assignees":[],"milestone":null,"comments":26,"created_at":"2020-07-31T22:02:39Z","updated_at":"2024-11-03T23:21:30Z","closed_at":"2024-05-07T12:03:02Z","assignee":null,"author_association":"NONE","type":null,"active_lock_reason":"resolved","sub_issues_summary":{"total":0,"completed":0,"percent_completed":0},"issue_dependencies_summary":{"blocked_by":0,"total_blocked_by":0,"blocking":0,"total_blocking":0},"body":"**What did you do?**\r\n\r\nI used PromConsole.Graph with `renderer: \"area\"`, and often see time series elevated more than they should be, as if they were stacked on other time series which are not actually under them.  I attach a screenshot.\r\n\r\nSee https://github.com/livebungalow/promconsole-rendering-example for a small working example (well, non-working, which is the point).  For the purposes of that example, I monkey-patch `PromConsole.Graph.prototype.buildQueryUrl` to inject data which provokes the issue -- I copied this data from an actual `query_range` response, formatted it, and reduced it to a manageable size.\r\n\r\n**What did you expect to see?**\r\n\r\nTime series resting on the x-axis.\r\n\r\n**What did you see instead? Under which circumstances?**\r\n\r\nTime series elevated off the x-axis.  The linked example repo has sample data that provokes the problem.\r\n\r\n**Environment**\r\n\r\nThe linked example uses the docker image `prom/prometheus:v2.19.3` with its standard configuration file.","closed_by":{"login":"beorn7","id":5609886,"node_id":"MDQ6VXNlcjU2MDk4ODY=","avatar_url":"https://avatars.githubusercontent.com/u/5609886?v=4","gravatar_id":"","url":"https://api.github.com/users/beorn7","html_url":"https://github.com/beorn7",